From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:06:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 15/48] net: airoha: xpon: re-arm the BER interval timer after
 a PHY down sample

G.984.3 has the ONU send one REI per BER interval while in O5. When
gpon_ber_timer_fn() found the PHY not ready or in LOS it queued
phy_link_work and returned without re-arming itself. The timer is only
re-armed by BER_interval (sent once per activation by the Huawei OLT),
by the O5 entry, or by itself; so if the link was back by the time
phy_link_work sampled it, there was no O6/O5 transition and REI stopped
for the rest of the session.

Re-arm the timer before skipping the report. A real loss still goes
O5 -> O6, which deletes the timer, and the timer function itself bails
out outside O5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index 260b674..0335521 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -3250,6 +3250,14 @@ static void gpon_ber_timer_fn(struct timer_list *t)
 
 	ret = airoha_xpon_phy_get_link_state(priv->phy, &ready, &los);
 	if (!ret && (!ready || los)) {
+		/*
+		 * Skip this report but keep the interval running: if the link
+		 * is back before phy_link_work samples it there is no O6/O5
+		 * transition to re-arm the timer, and REI would stop for the
+		 * rest of the session. On a real loss O6 deletes it again.
+		 */
+		mod_timer(&priv->ber_timer,
+			  jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(priv->ber_interval_ms));
 		mod_delayed_work(priv->fsm_wq, &priv->phy_link_work, 0);
 		return;
 	}
